## Difference Array vs Line Sweep

Difference array:

```text
Uses an array of size N.
Works when coordinates are small and bounded.
```

Line sweep:

```text
Stores only event points.
Works when coordinates are huge (up to 10^9 or more).
```

Difference array:

```text
Space: O(N)
```

Line sweep:

```text
Space: O(Q)
```

where `Q` is the number of intervals.

---

## Coordinate Compression + Line Sweep

When coordinates are large but many queries exist:

1. Collect all unique coordinates.
2. Sort them.
3. Map coordinates to compressed indices.
4. Apply difference array / prefix sum on compressed indices.

Pattern:

```text
Large coordinates + many updates
⇒ Coordinate Compression + Line Sweep
```

